{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1858"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge earth-space/oceans","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/earth-space__oceans.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",996],["+","The broadest of all coastal shapes is the bay, a wide indentation where the sea reaches into the land, called a gulf when it is especially large. The biggest of them all is the Bay of Bengal, some 2.2 million square kilometres of the north-eastern Indian Ocean between India, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh and Myanmar. Into its head the Ganges and the Brahmaputra pour so much sediment that they have built the largest delta on Earth, whose mangrove forests, the Sundarbans, are home to the Bengal tiger.\n\n"],["=",97],["+","\n| bay | the sea's reach into the land | Bay of Bengal |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",942],["+","Die weiteste aller Küstenformen ist die Bucht, eine breite Einbuchtung, in der das Meer ins Land hineinreicht und die man, wenn sie besonders groß ist, Golf nennt. Die größte von allen ist der Golf von Bengalen, rund 2,2 Millionen Quadratkilometer des nordöstlichen Indischen Ozeans zwischen Indien, Sri Lanka, Bangladesch und Myanmar. In sein Ende schütten Ganges und Brahmaputra so viel Sediment, dass sie das größte Delta der Erde aufgebaut haben, dessen Mangrovenwälder, die Sundarbans, die Heimat des Bengalischen Tigers sind.\n\n"],["=",91],["+","\n| Bucht | Einbuchtung des Meeres | Golf von Bengalen |"]]}]},
